First, let's calculate the price per ounce of the 48-ounce size. The price is \$3.90 for 48 ounces.

$$
\text{Price per ounce} = \frac{\$3.90}{48 \text{ ounces}} = 0.08125 \text{ dollars per ounce}
$$

Next, we want the price per ounce of the 32-ounce size to be 25% more than the price per ounce of the 48-ounce size.

$$
