Wait, but what if one of the functions is zero? Well, even functions can be zero. But even if f(x) is zero everywhere, then f(x)g(x) would be zero, which is even. Because zero is even. Similarly, if both are zero, the product is zero, which is even. 

Therefore, regardless of the specific even functions, their product will be even. So the answer is even.
