To answer the question, you need to first understand what an even function is. An even function is a function that is symmetric with respect to the y-axis. This means that for any x, $ f(-x) = f(x) $. 

Given that $ f(x) $ and $ g(x) $ are both even functions, we can use their properties to determine the nature of $ f(x)g(x) $.

Let’s compute $ f(-x)g(-x) $, which is the function evaluated at -x. Since both $ f $ and $ g $ are even, $ f(-x) = f(x) $ and $ g(-x) = g(x) $. Therefore, $ f(-x)g(-x) = f(x)g(x) $. 

This means that $ f(x)g(x) $ is equal to itself when evaluated at -x, which is the definition of an even function. 

So, the product of two even functions is also an even function.
The product of two even functions is even.

$$
f(-x)g(-x) = f(x)g(x)
$$

This satisfies the definition of an even function.

