To simplify the expression 
$$\sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{4}{\sqrt{24}}+\dfrac{\sqrt{3456}}{9}+\sqrt{6}}{\sqrt{6}}},$$
we follow these steps:

Step 1: Simplify each term inside the numerator:

a. $\dfrac{4}{\sqrt{24}}$: 
$$
\dfrac{4}{\sqrt{24}} = \dfrac{4}{2\sqrt{6}} = \dfrac{2}{\sqrt{6}} = \dfrac{2\sqrt{6}}{6} = \dfrac{\sqrt{6}}{3}
$$

b. $\dfrac{\sqrt{3456}}{9}$: 
$$
\sqrt{3456} = \sqrt{144 \cdot 24} = \sqrt{144} \cdot \sqrt{24} = 12 \cdot 2\sqrt{6} = 24\sqrt{6}
$$
$$
\dfrac{24\sqrt{6}}{9} = \dfrac{8\sqrt{6}}{3}
$$

c. $\sqrt{6}$ remains as is.

Step 2: Combine the simplified terms in the numerator:

$$
\dfrac{\sqrt{6}}{3} + \dfrac{8\sqrt{6}}{3} + \sqrt{6} = \dfrac{\sqrt{6}}{3} + \dfrac{8\sqrt{6}}{3} + \dfrac{3\sqrt{6}}{3} = \dfrac{(1 + 8 + 3)\sqrt{6}}{3} = \dfrac{12\sqrt{6}}{3} = 4\sqrt{6}
$$

Step 3: Simplify the entire fraction:

$$
\dfrac{4\sqrt{6}}{\sqrt{6}} = 4
$$

Step 4: Take the square root of the result:

$$
\sqrt{4} = 2
$$

