$$
C(4, 2) = \frac{4!}{2! \cdot (4-2)!} = \frac{4 \cdot 3}{2 \cdot 1} = 6
$$

To find the total number of ways to select 3 boys and 2 girls, we multiply the two values:
$$
35 \times 6 = 210
$$

