### Step 2: Consider All Possible Combinations

Let’s compute $ a^2 \mod{3} $ and $ b^2 \mod{3} $ in each case.

| $ a \mod{3} $ | $ a^2 \mod{3} $ |
|----------------|-------------------|
| 1              | $ 1^2 = 1 \mod{3} $ |
| 2              | $ 2^2 = 4 \equiv 1 \mod{3} $ |

