Next, the problem says this volume is increased by 19 cubic centimeters. So I need to add 19 to the original volume. That would be 8 + 19. Let me do that math: 8 + 19 is 27. So the new volume of the larger cube is 27 cubic centimeters.

Now, the question is asking for the length of one edge of the new cube. Since it's a cube, all edges are equal, so if I can find the cube root of the new volume, that will give me the length of each edge. So let me compute the cube root of 27. Hmm, cube root of 27 is 3 because 3*3*3 is 27. Therefore, the edge length of the new cube is 3 centimeters.

